WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.325 --> 00:00:02.321
- I didn't go into this to prove

00:00:02.321 --> 00:00:05.578
anything to anybody other than myself.

00:00:05.578 --> 00:00:08.035
There was a lot of raised eyebrows.

00:00:08.035 --> 00:00:09.947
All those that could raise their eyebrows.

00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:11.893
(laughter)

00:00:11.893 --> 00:00:14.548
When they heard I was going to do this.

00:00:14.548 --> 00:00:17.129
Pop star who's married to a footballer,

00:00:17.129 --> 00:00:19.027
really going to do a clothing line?

00:00:19.027 --> 00:00:22.664
When someone kicks me, I
try hard to get up again.

00:00:22.664 --> 00:00:24.282
- She an English entrepreneur,

00:00:24.282 --> 00:00:26.674
fashion designer, model, and singer.

00:00:26.674 --> 00:00:30.087
She rose to fame with the all
female pop group Spice Girls.

00:00:30.087 --> 00:00:31.475
In the past decade she's become an

00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:35.272
internationally recognized
fashion icon and designer.

00:00:35.272 --> 00:00:36.971
She's Victoria Beckham, and here's my

00:00:36.971 --> 00:00:39.124
take on her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:39.124 --> 00:00:40.976
Number one is my personal favorite and

00:00:40.976 --> 00:00:42.948
I'd love to know which one
you guys like the best.

00:00:42.948 --> 00:00:44.467
Also as she's talking,
if she says something

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.619
that really impacts you, please leave it

00:00:46.619 --> 00:00:48.286
in the comments below
and put quotes around it

00:00:48.286 --> 00:00:50.767
so that other people
can be inspired as well.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:51.600
Enjoy.

00:00:54.861 --> 00:00:58.361
(upbeat orchestral music)

00:01:05.173 --> 00:01:06.741
- It is what I always wanted to do,

00:01:06.741 --> 00:01:09.356
fashion really is my passion, it's what

00:01:09.356 --> 00:01:13.017
I love to do, it's what I have to do.

00:01:13.017 --> 00:01:17.806
I love what I do, I don't
consider what I do as my job.

00:01:17.806 --> 00:01:20.764
I always say well it's almost like,

00:01:20.764 --> 00:01:22.970
it almost feels like a hobby that

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:27.253
has done really really
well because I love it.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.538
A lot of people don't associate work with

00:01:29.538 --> 00:01:32.194
enjoying themselves and
they don't associate

00:01:32.194 --> 00:01:35.172
work with being their
passion whereas I really do.

00:01:35.172 --> 00:01:37.896
But fashion was always my passion,

00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:41.004
and I'm living a dream, I really am,

00:01:41.004 --> 00:01:44.322
and I wake up every
morning and I pinch myself.

00:01:44.322 --> 00:01:46.258
I'm very very lucky, I feel very blessed,

00:01:46.258 --> 00:01:49.486
so I would say right now is definitely

00:01:49.486 --> 00:01:52.171
where I feel comfortable, I believe that

00:01:52.171 --> 00:01:54.754
I'm competing in an arena where

00:01:56.657 --> 00:02:00.252
actually, I feel like I'm good at this,

00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:01.877
I've got a long way to go, there's lots

00:02:01.877 --> 00:02:03.793
of things that I want to do, I was

00:02:03.793 --> 00:02:05.287
never going to be the best singer or

00:02:05.287 --> 00:02:07.644
the best dancer, and that was okay.

00:02:07.644 --> 00:02:09.493
I had four other people with me.

00:02:09.493 --> 00:02:10.856
- You did quite well at it through.

00:02:10.856 --> 00:02:14.373
- I didn't do bad, but I hid behind

00:02:14.373 --> 00:02:16.324
the others a little bit, but I really

00:02:16.324 --> 00:02:18.762
feel that I had something to give,

00:02:18.762 --> 00:02:21.601
I feel that I have a point of view,

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:24.313
and I have a lot to say, and it's

00:02:24.313 --> 00:02:26.082
great when you find something that

00:02:26.082 --> 00:02:29.092
you think that you're okay at.

00:02:29.092 --> 00:02:31.283
I say the best advice that I could

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:34.257
give anybody is to work for somebody else.

00:02:34.257 --> 00:02:36.478
Work for another brand, and when I

00:02:36.478 --> 00:02:38.403
was working with Rock &amp; Republic,

00:02:38.403 --> 00:02:39.921
when I was working with Linda Farrow

00:02:39.921 --> 00:02:41.941
which is a sunglasses brand that

00:02:41.941 --> 00:02:45.982
I was working for, I was like a sponge.

00:02:45.982 --> 00:02:48.724
You can take that opportunity to learn

00:02:48.724 --> 00:02:52.288
so much about the
industry, and I did that.

00:02:52.288 --> 00:02:54.024
They were licensed deals that I had

00:02:54.024 --> 00:02:55.949
back in the day, and I worked with

00:02:55.949 --> 00:02:59.524
Koti, the fragrance company, the fragrance

00:02:59.524 --> 00:03:02.607
house as well, and I learned so much.

00:03:03.443 --> 00:03:05.694
When I was in a position
to bring everything

00:03:05.694 --> 00:03:08.755
in house and own everything myself and

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:11.229
create a team that would do this

00:03:11.229 --> 00:03:14.631
with me, I felt ready to do it.

00:03:14.631 --> 00:03:16.052
Though I didn't really, I didn't

00:03:16.052 --> 00:03:18.300
go to fashion school, I was working

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.415
for other people and I learned an

00:03:20.415 --> 00:03:25.069
enormous amount in a
very short space of time.

00:03:25.069 --> 00:03:27.065
I always want to better myself.

00:03:27.065 --> 00:03:29.719
I don't consider myself, sorry, I don't

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:32.922
consider other designers competition.

00:03:32.922 --> 00:03:36.127
For me, my competition is
me from the season before.

00:03:36.127 --> 00:03:37.971
I'm very ambitious, I always want

00:03:37.971 --> 00:03:40.085
to better myself, I never sit back and

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:42.595
say wow, look at what I've achieved.

00:03:42.595 --> 00:03:44.882
To be honest I wish that I could do that

00:03:44.882 --> 00:03:48.131
because I should do that, but I always

00:03:48.131 --> 00:03:50.603
just want to better myself, what's next,

00:03:50.603 --> 00:03:54.022
how can I improve, how
can I make myself better?

00:03:54.022 --> 00:03:57.675
I'm a perfectionist, but in
the nicest sense of the word.

00:03:57.675 --> 00:03:59.862
I was going to say that I think there are

00:03:59.862 --> 00:04:01.563
a lot of celebrities that have a lot

00:04:01.563 --> 00:04:03.730
of clothing lines or perfumes, and I

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.234
think that what I'm
doing is very different,

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.706
I'm not just putting my
name on different products.

00:04:08.706 --> 00:04:11.460
I'm very involved, I go to the factories,

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.710
I see the denim, I work with the people

00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:17.948
that I'm working with, and I think that's

00:04:17.948 --> 00:04:20.148
what makes what I'm doing
very very different.

00:04:20.148 --> 00:04:23.288
I'm creative director,
I've been working on

00:04:23.288 --> 00:04:25.730
everything that I'm working on now

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.502
for the last seven years, this has

00:04:27.502 --> 00:04:29.598
been a long, long process and that's

00:04:29.598 --> 00:04:31.812
how long it's taken to get it right.

00:04:31.812 --> 00:04:33.630
I'm not just saying I'm Victoria Beckham,

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:36.140
I'm going to put my name
on a bottle of perfume.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.865
I'm actually creating that, I'm designing

00:04:38.865 --> 00:04:41.285
the bottle, I'm designing the label and

00:04:41.285 --> 00:04:44.201
that's what I love,
that's my fourth child.

00:04:44.201 --> 00:04:47.368
When I initially started up the brand,

00:04:48.924 --> 00:04:50.471
I didn't put too much pressure on myself,

00:04:50.471 --> 00:04:52.344
I didn't go into this to prove

00:04:52.344 --> 00:04:55.474
anything to anybody other than myself.

00:04:55.474 --> 00:04:57.122
I was very focused, I didn't try

00:04:57.122 --> 00:05:00.122
and do everything at once, for quite

00:05:00.963 --> 00:05:03.401
a few seasons I stopped to just

00:05:03.401 --> 00:05:05.849
perfecting the dress, I didn't

00:05:05.849 --> 00:05:08.146
want to run before I could walk.

00:05:08.146 --> 00:05:09.667
It's very important to be focused

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:12.834
and do what I was doing very very well

00:05:13.902 --> 00:05:16.485
and move on and do more when my

00:05:17.358 --> 00:05:20.358
team was in the position to do that.

00:05:21.344 --> 00:05:25.006
I think that it's about
keeping things focused.

00:05:25.006 --> 00:05:27.047
I'm not trying to do too much.

00:05:27.047 --> 00:05:29.378
- You didn't care what people
say, what people think of you.

00:05:29.378 --> 00:05:31.169
- No, I mean I gave up a long long time

00:05:31.169 --> 00:05:34.507
worrying and concerning myself over that.

00:05:34.507 --> 00:05:37.016
I care what people say about what I do

00:05:37.016 --> 00:05:40.608
professionally, I care
about what my customer says.

00:05:40.608 --> 00:05:42.974
That's what I do care about because

00:05:42.974 --> 00:05:45.567
why do I do what I do, I do what I do

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:48.692
because I love women, I
want to empower women,

00:05:48.692 --> 00:05:50.710
I want women to feel good, I want them

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:53.322
to feel beautiful, and so I care about

00:05:53.322 --> 00:05:55.349
what my customer thinks because I

00:05:55.349 --> 00:05:57.464
want to give her what she wants,

00:05:57.464 --> 00:05:58.915
but generally speaking, I don't

00:05:58.915 --> 00:06:01.915
focus too much on anything negative.

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:06.161
When I first started, so 10 seasons ago,

00:06:07.629 --> 00:06:10.629
I had a room at a hotel in New York,

00:06:12.655 --> 00:06:15.219
and I did sometimes one
on one presentations,

00:06:15.219 --> 00:06:16.712
sometimes as a group of people,

00:06:16.712 --> 00:06:18.918
sometimes it was one on one, and I

00:06:18.918 --> 00:06:22.918
did that for four days
to fashion press, buyers.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.509
I literally would talk
through the collection,

00:06:28.509 --> 00:06:31.288
I had 10 dresses and I'd sit there and

00:06:31.288 --> 00:06:33.000
I'd talk about the dress and the dress

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.628
would come in on a model and I'd unzip

00:06:34.628 --> 00:06:36.538
the dress and talk about the corsetry

00:06:36.538 --> 00:06:39.518
and the inspiration and the fabrics.

00:06:39.518 --> 00:06:41.439
Sometimes I'd be talking
for hours on end to

00:06:41.439 --> 00:06:43.523
people that didn't actually
even speak English.

00:06:43.523 --> 00:06:44.828
(laughter)

00:06:44.828 --> 00:06:46.287
They were foreign retailers, but I

00:06:46.287 --> 00:06:48.355
just like to talk, so I'd be talking away

00:06:48.355 --> 00:06:51.288
and really wanted people to understand the

00:06:51.288 --> 00:06:56.006
concept really and
understand what I was doing.

00:06:56.006 --> 00:06:57.885
I remember it was 3 o'clock in the morning

00:06:57.885 --> 00:06:59.658
the night before the
show and I was standing,

00:06:59.658 --> 00:07:01.854
there was a florist actually in the hotel

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.850
and I was standing there in my slippers

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:05.936
trying to decide on the flowers.

00:07:05.936 --> 00:07:07.793
I didn't have a stylist or great

00:07:07.793 --> 00:07:09.241
hair and makeup, things have come

00:07:09.241 --> 00:07:11.991
such a long way since those days.

00:07:14.452 --> 00:07:16.565
I think right at the beginning, I didn't

00:07:16.565 --> 00:07:18.269
know what people were going to think,

00:07:18.269 --> 00:07:20.731
there was a lot of raised eyebrows.

00:07:20.731 --> 00:07:22.728
All those that could raise their eyebrows.

00:07:22.728 --> 00:07:24.726
(laughter)

00:07:24.726 --> 00:07:27.308
When they heard I was going to do this.

00:07:27.308 --> 00:07:29.824
Pop star who's married to a footballer

00:07:29.824 --> 00:07:32.714
really going to do a clothing line?

00:07:32.714 --> 00:07:35.631
A lot of people had preconceptions.

00:07:37.481 --> 00:07:39.047
I didn't go out to prove
anybody wrong, I just

00:07:39.047 --> 00:07:41.162
wanted to prove to myself
that I could do it.

00:07:41.162 --> 00:07:43.310
- And what comes to is your determination

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:46.055
at all cost to actually succeed, I mean

00:07:46.055 --> 00:07:48.098
is that a message that
you hope comes across

00:07:48.098 --> 00:07:50.269
to kids because a lot of kids think that

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:52.807
people just become famous
overnight don't they?

00:07:52.807 --> 00:07:54.638
- Yeah, I think that people don't realize

00:07:54.638 --> 00:07:56.492
that it's all about hard work, I mean

00:07:56.492 --> 00:07:58.706
I worked hard when I was at school,

00:07:58.706 --> 00:08:00.309
I've always had it in my personality

00:08:00.309 --> 00:08:02.845
to want to succeed, even when it was

00:08:02.845 --> 00:08:05.262
I want to do my homework right.

00:08:06.596 --> 00:08:08.082
But yeah, I'm one of these people,

00:08:08.082 --> 00:08:11.771
when someone kicks me, I
try hard to get up again.

00:08:11.771 --> 00:08:13.265
Because I know what I want to do, I love

00:08:13.265 --> 00:08:14.875
what I do at the end of the day, I know

00:08:14.875 --> 00:08:16.720
that I'm putting myself up for criticism,

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.690
I'm very much aware of
that, but I love what I do.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:22.857
I think everybody has crazy moments of

00:08:25.169 --> 00:08:27.472
self-doubt, and I think that an element

00:08:27.472 --> 00:08:31.196
of that is probably quite important.

00:08:31.196 --> 00:08:33.950
It's about creative visualization and

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.938
challenging yourself, but always

00:08:35.938 --> 00:08:37.837
staying very positive, and there's

00:08:37.837 --> 00:08:39.967
nothing wrong with having a second

00:08:39.967 --> 00:08:42.957
little person sitting on your shoulder

00:08:42.957 --> 00:08:46.277
making sure that you are remaining humble

00:08:46.277 --> 00:08:49.580
and that you're remaining appreciative

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:51.426
of everything that you have and

00:08:51.426 --> 00:08:54.601
everything that you've achieved.

00:08:54.601 --> 00:08:55.725
You should definitely not waste

00:08:55.725 --> 00:08:57.130
too much time being negative in

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:59.640
any way, it's about positive thinking,

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:03.807
positive energy, and fighting
if you need to fight.

00:09:04.971 --> 00:09:06.992
I mean my team is so great, we're a

00:09:06.992 --> 00:09:08.962
small team, but we're growing and

00:09:08.962 --> 00:09:11.117
they're all incredibly talented,

00:09:11.117 --> 00:09:13.777
passionate, focused, I also think

00:09:13.777 --> 00:09:15.530
it's important to enjoy the people

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:16.987
that you're working with as well.

00:09:16.987 --> 00:09:20.039
We have a lot of fun every day,

00:09:20.039 --> 00:09:21.343
but they're passionate, they love

00:09:21.343 --> 00:09:23.540
what they do, they believe in my

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.502
brand and what I'm creating.

00:09:26.502 --> 00:09:28.047
I have the same team that I had

00:09:28.047 --> 00:09:30.801
when I first started over six years ago.

00:09:30.801 --> 00:09:32.793
I really encourage my team to grow

00:09:32.793 --> 00:09:36.149
with me as I grow as a brand as well.

00:09:36.149 --> 00:09:37.949
Yes, I bring in a few new people,

00:09:37.949 --> 00:09:40.269
but it's about giving people that

00:09:40.269 --> 00:09:42.268
work with me the opportunity to

00:09:42.268 --> 00:09:44.715
grow within the company as well.

00:09:44.715 --> 00:09:45.909
I have a few people that started

00:09:45.909 --> 00:09:48.251
out with me as interns that now have

00:09:48.251 --> 00:09:52.418
high up jobs in marketing,
press, and sales as well.

00:09:56.602 --> 00:10:00.276
It's a really nice family
atmosphere at work.

00:10:00.276 --> 00:10:01.878
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:10:01.878 --> 00:10:03.848
I made this video because Kris Dunlop

00:10:03.848 --> 00:10:05.349
asked me to, so if there's a famous

00:10:05.349 --> 00:10:06.924
entrepreneur that you want me to profile

00:10:06.924 --> 00:10:08.282
next, leave it down in the comments

00:10:08.282 --> 00:10:09.983
below and I'll see what I can do.

00:10:09.983 --> 00:10:11.405
I'd also love to know what did

00:10:11.405 --> 00:10:13.565
you learn from Victoria in this video,

00:10:13.565 --> 00:10:14.682
what's the thing that you're going to

00:10:14.682 --> 00:10:16.688
apply immediately to your life or

00:10:16.688 --> 00:10:18.948
your business after watching this clip?

00:10:18.948 --> 00:10:20.664
Super curious to find out, leave it in the

00:10:20.664 --> 00:10:22.809
comments, I'm going to
join in the discussion.

00:10:22.809 --> 00:10:24.384
I also want to give a quick shout-out

00:10:24.384 --> 00:10:26.298
to Sandra from Kitsch Cakes, Sandra thank

00:10:26.298 --> 00:10:28.026
you so much for picking
up a copy of my book,

00:10:28.026 --> 00:10:30.626
Your One Word, and making those awesome

00:10:30.626 --> 00:10:33.884
tribute cookies, they looked amazing

00:10:33.884 --> 00:10:35.674
and they tasted even better and I

00:10:35.674 --> 00:10:39.966
really really really
appreciate your support.

00:10:39.966 --> 00:10:41.188
- Tada!

00:10:41.188 --> 00:10:43.527
This is what we've made for you.

00:10:43.527 --> 00:10:46.860
In tribute to your #Believe, here we go.

00:10:47.945 --> 00:10:49.591
- Thank you guys again for watching.

00:10:49.591 --> 00:10:51.405
I believe in you, I hope you continue

00:10:51.405 --> 00:10:53.645
to believe in yourself and whatever

00:10:53.645 --> 00:10:56.139
your one word is, much love.

00:10:56.139 --> 00:10:57.639
I'll see you soon.

